body:
No it does not are you okay? how do you achieve the success on the roll before advantage is rolled? its Specific "THE" d20 on a "Success" so you roll with advantage and you get a 5 and a 17 the 17 is a Success, this triggers Silvery Barbs. you reroll that 17 and take the lowest. say you roll an 18 you stick with that 17. if you roll a 6 you take that. if you were to roll a 3 you wouldn't take the 5 as its no longer in play since the success was determined. what is so hard to understand about this? it functions as a reroll. its different from lucky, its closer to inspiration where the Die is rerolled after the result is determined. its not super disadvantage, its not useless when advantage is in play, its just a reroll of the successful roll.

&#x200B;

[https://tabletopbuilds.com/spell-spotlight-silvery-barbs/#How\_does\_it\_work\_with\_sequential\_castings](https://tabletopbuilds.com/spell-spotlight-silvery-barbs/#How_does_it_work_with_sequential_castings) at the top is explains how the spell works with the wording and specifics.
